-- title:
--   Round six: the per-bit cost is O(lg^{1-gap} polylog)
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ satisfy `Prm.Ok`. The round-six per-bit cost is
--
--   $$N(P,n) = d + \ell d^{\lambda'} + d p^{\delta} + (\ell + \log_2 p) + p^{\delta} + \ell (d \ln p)^{\tau} + 1$$
--
--   with the parameter map of `params6_ok`. Then there are constants $C \ge 0$, $A \in \mathbb N$ and $n_1$ such that for all $n \ge n_1$
--
--   $$N(P, n) \le C\, (\lg n)^{1 - \mathrm{gap}(P)}\, (\log \lg n + 1)^{A}.$$
--
--   Combined with $V \le 48n$ this yields running time $O(n \lg^{1-\mathrm{gap}} n\,\mathrm{polylog})$ for a machine whose time per bit is bounded by $N$.
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.Ncost6_le (P : Prm) (hP : P.Ok) : ∃ (C : ℝ) (A : ℕ) (n₁ : ℕ), 0 ≤ C ∧ ∀ n, n₁ ≤ n →
--       Ncost6 P n ≤ C * (IntMul.lg n : ℝ) ^ (1 - P.gap) * (Real.log (IntMul.lg n) + 1) ^ A
--   ```
